 "conditions": [
  {
   "id": "rated_voltage_v",
   "label": "Rated at output voltage",
   "type": "number",
   "unit": "V",
   "description": "Review 3: the output voltage a rated (delivered) capacity was measured at (5 V). Basis condition of cap.rated_mah, so a 5 V/3 A figure and a 5 V/2.1 A figure are never one comparable cohort."
  },
  {
   "id": "rated_current_a",
   "label": "Rated at load current",
   "type": "number",
   "unit": "A",
   "description": "The load current of the rated-capacity test ('5V/3A' -> 3). A rating without a printed load stays an unresolved preview claim."
  },
  {
   "id": "energy_basis",
   "label": "Energy figure basis",
   "type": "enum",
   "enum": [
    "rated",
    "typical"
   ],
   "description": "r7 (A2 2026-11-24): basis of a cap.energy_wh figure when the maker prints a typical/rated PAIR and labels each one. Set only from the printed label; a single unlabelled figure carries no condition, and an unlabelled pair stays an unresolved preview claim."
  },
  {
   "id": "basis",
   "label": "Value basis",
   "type": "enum",
   "enum": [
    "complete_enumeration",
    "derived"
   ],
   "description": "A1 ruling 1 (coordinator, 2026-11-24): a negative (pd.pps false) is written ONLY when the maker's own structured spec section prints a complete list for the unit (every output port with its protocol list) and none names the feature. The claim carries basis=complete_enumeration and keeps that list as raw. Prose, marketing bullets, partial tables, 'etc.' lists, PDO-only lists and missing rows never produce a negative. derived (r7 coordinator ruling, 2026-11-26): pd.pps true, kind derived, when the maker names Samsung Super Fast Charging 2.0 or '45W for Samsung' for that SKU (SFC 2.0 is PPS by definition); never a PPS range (claim/derive-samsung-sfc2-pps@1)."
  }
 ],
